.TH ifg-api 1  "ifg-api 0.9.0" 
.SH NAME
ifg\-api \- Raw pass\-through to the IronForge REST API (paths relative to /api/v1/)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg api\fR [\fB\-X\fR|\fB\-\-method\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-field\fR] [\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-\-paginate\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Raw pass\-through to the IronForge REST API (paths relative to /api/v1/)
.PP
Long\-tail endpoints (wiki, webhooks, packages, secrets, runners) work here until they get first\-class commands. `\-f key=value` sends a JSON field, `\-\-input file` sends a raw body, and `\-\-paginate` merges the `data` arrays of every page into one array (GET only).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-X\fR, \fB\-\-method\fR \fI<METHOD>\fR [default: GET]
HTTP method (default GET)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-field\fR \fI<KEY=VALUE>\fR
Add a field. With GET these become query parameters; with other methods they form a JSON body of strings
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read the JSON request body from a file ("\-" for stdin)
.TP
\fB\-\-paginate\fR
Follow pagination and merge all `data` arrays into one JSON array
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path relative to /api/v1/, e.g. "users/me"
.SH VERSION
v0.9.0
